From 5bc0e529e0d2afc9fab049be12e78a4131ab3798 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Neanderfunk <projekt@neanderfunk.de>
Date: Tue, 15 Sep 2026 08:19:18 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] batadv: count each originator once, not each route

Bytes 2-3 of the batman_adv information element are what the NodeMonitor app
shows as "Knoten im Netz" / nodes in the network. They were incremented for
every entry of the BATADV_CMD_GET_ORIGINATORS dump - but that dump has one
entry per originator, next hop and hard interface. A node heard through
several neighbours over 2.4 GHz, 5 GHz and the VPN is counted once per path.

Measured on a Gluon v2023.2 node (Archer C25, 9 neighbours): 332 entries in
the originator table, 91 distinct originators; the app showed 338. 43 of the
originators were known via 5 paths, 5 via 9.

Count only the entry batman flags with BATADV_ATTR_FLAG_BEST - exactly one per
originator. The neighbour count (bytes 4-5) is unchanged: it counts direct
links, one per neighbour and interface, like "batctl n". Wire format and app
stay as they are.
---
 src/batadv.c | 6 +++++-
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/batadv.c b/src/batadv.c
index 4e3ddcc..0ca83dc 100644
--- a/src/batadv.c
+++ b/src/batadv.c
@@ -87,7 +87,11 @@ static int parse_orig_list_netlink_cb(struct nl_msg *msg, void *arg)
 	if (if_indextoname(hardif, ifname) == NULL)
 		return NL_OK;
 
-	opts->stats->originator_count++;
+	/* The dump has one entry per originator AND next hop AND interface: a
+	 * node heard through five neighbours shows up five times. Count each
+	 * originator once, on the entry batman marks as its best next hop. */
+	if (attrs[BATADV_ATTR_FLAG_BEST])
+		opts->stats->originator_count++;
 	if (memcmp(orig, dest, 6) != 0)
 		return NL_OK;
 
